{
  "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
  "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:09 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Tenth Circuit in this case correctly held that Stone could not share in the award given by the jury unless he was an original source of pondcrete allegations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Ms. Mahoney, let me ask you a question. Am I wrong about this? It seems to me that if he was not an original source, not only shouldn't he get any money, but neither should the government. Isn't that the way the statute reads?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the way that the courts have handled it below is that it says that there's no jurisdiction unless it is a claim brought by a relator who is an original source or if it's brought by the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Otherwise, the Attorney General could just bring it all over again, a fresh complaint, and that would be wasted motion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But you'd then have to pay his attorneys' fees. That's what really this is about, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He left his job in March of 1986. How could he possibly have direct and independent knowledge of those predicate acts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: What was the public disclosure of the claim that ultimately prevailed?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. VULLO",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. VULLO: Mr. Stone did not testify at trial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It might be natural for the Court to wonder, why would it be in the government's interest to advocate that a share of the money damages in this case should be given to a private party."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart (Government)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One of the features of this case that may appear anomalous is the fact that the government is aligned with Stone. That is, it's Rockwell's position that the entire recovery in this case should go to the United States. It is Stone's position that the recovery should be shared with the relator, and the government agrees with Stone."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Explain why it would be a minor variation if what he has identified as a defect in the pipe system and what turns out to be the situation that was covered up is the inadequate cement that caused the loss?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF MAUREEN E. MAHONEY ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Mahoney (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He didn't know anything about fraud and he couldn't have known they were leaking at the time, 5 years later because he wasn't there. And the statute requires direct knowledge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: There were other documents. He said there were other documents and the district court said sorry, you came up with that too late, I'm not going to look at the other documents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Mahoney",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8f647debb851d99d5b89793fb4a7b0c7061a53ba8c9284bbc133a8f02a76ef41",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8f647debb851-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MAHONEY: Your Honor, what they're referring to is the affidavit, I think. He filed an affidavit at the outset of the case when Rockwell filed the motion to dismiss and then tried to do a new one 10 years later that was rejected."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1272",
      "confidence": 0.0,
